## Infrastructure Issues & Limitations

1. SPOF (Single Point of Failure): Since everything runs on a single server (Nginx, Application Server, and MySQL), if the hardware fails or any critical component crashes, the entire website goes offline instantly.
2. Downtime During Maintenance: Any deployment of new code or software updates requires restarting components like the web server or application server, causing service interruption for users.
3. Lack of Scalability: A single server has finite CPU, RAM, and disk IO resources. It cannot handle vertical scaling beyond its hardware limits and cannot scale horizontally to distribute high incoming traffic.
